course: dictionary
lesson: 4900
title: Illness and being unwell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An illness is a disease, or a time when you are ill. Some illnesses are mild, like a cold, and some are serious. «Off school because of illness» means a child was too unwell to come in. Here illness names something that happens to a person.
explain: Illness can also mean the state of being unwell, like when you feel poorly. Illness is uncountable in this sense, so you do not say «an illness» for the feeling. You say «suffering from illness» or «recover from illness». Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Before a vaccination you can tell the nurse you are scared» shows that doctors and nurses help keep people from serious illness. Some illnesses spread by germs, so washing hands, covering coughs and staying home when ill help stop them.
fact: An illness is a disease, or a time of being ill.
fact: Illness, with no «a» before it, means the state of being unwell.
fact: «A serious illness» is one that can be very dangerous, and doctors, nurses and medicines help treat it.
fact: Some illnesses are infectious, which means they spread by germs from person to person.
fact: «Recover from an illness» means get better after being ill.
exercise: In «an illness of the brain called dementia», what does illness mean? | A place where doctors work | A kind of medicine that makes you better | *A disease that affects the body or mind
exercise: «The vaccine protects you from serious illness.» What does illness mean here? | *Being seriously unwell with a disease | A cold day at school | A kind of sweet | A brave feeling
exercise: Find and copy one word from «A&E is for serious injuries and illnesses» that means more than one illness. | injuries | A&E | serious | *illnesses
test: «Mia stayed home from school because of illness.» What does illness mean here? | Being in a hurry | *Being unwell | Being on holiday | Being very tall
test: Which phrase from the lesson means getting better after being ill? | *Recover from an illness | Paint a picture | Build a wall | Ride a bike
exam: Ben says «A&E» is a doctor's name. Using the context «A&E is for serious injuries and illnesses», what is the right answer? | A&E is a medicine for coughs | *A&E is the place where serious injuries and illnesses are treated | A&E is a doctor who visits homes | A&E is a school subject
